                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Editorial Note</hi></head>
                <p>On February 9, in accordance with a discussion between Acheson and Lovett on the
                    previous day, it was determined that Vice Chief of Staff, United States Army,
                    General Hull and U. Alexis Johnson would go to Japan and Korea to discuss and
                    explore the prisoner of war problem with the men on the spot. Hull and Johnson
                    left Washington for the Far East on February 11 and returned on February 22. An
                    account of their trip is reported in the memorandum for the record, March 10,
                        <ref target="#pg76">page 76</ref>.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
